        "text": "that we executed earlier.\nI\nI /sbin (system binaries): This directory contains system binary files that\nserve as administrative commands (e.g., fdisk ).\nI\nI / boot : This directory contains the Linux bootloader files.\nI\nI / dev (devices): This directory contains the device configuration files\n(e.g., /dev/null ).\nI\nI / sys : This is similar to /dev , which contains configurations about devices\nand drivers.\nI\nI / etc (etcetera): This directory contains all the administration system files\n(e.g., /etc/passwd shows all the system users in Kali).\nI\nI / lib (libraries): This directory contains the shared libraries for the binaries\ninside /bin and /sbin .\nI\nI / proc (processes): This directory holds the processes and kernel information\nfiles.\nChapter 1 I Mastering the Terminal Window\n3\nI\nI / lost+found : As the name says, this directory contains the files that have\nbeen recovered.",
